# cases the spirv-vk12 column cannot serve: a case name per line, then the reason.
# the column is spirv under `env = "vulkan1.2"` with the device features most cases
# need, so it refuses what SKIPS.spirv refuses and for the same reasons: every
# entry is a TARGET LIMITATION of SPIR-V itself, which no env or feature lifts,
# and its full reason is the matching line of SKIPS.spirv. a refusal this column
# makes and the spirv column does not is a defect of the env, not a line here.
#
# 85 of the 115 cases build, validate and carry the column. MACH DEFECT is empty.

# ---- TARGET LIMITATION ----

call/call_recursive  a self-recursive call graph, as SKIPS.spirv.
call/call_arg_capture  a plain module-scope variable, as SKIPS.spirv.
call/call_chain  a self-recursive call graph, as SKIPS.spirv.
call/call_indirect  a function value as a parameter, as SKIPS.spirv.
cmp/short_circuit  a plain module-scope variable, as SKIPS.spirv.
ct/by_memory  an #[oblivious] function, as SKIPS.spirv.
ct/mul_serial  an #[oblivious] function, as SKIPS.spirv.
ct/mul_secret  a secret multiply operand, as SKIPS.spirv.
ct/mul_secret128  a 128-bit integer, as SKIPS.spirv.
ct/shift_secret  a secret variable shift count, as SKIPS.spirv.
int128/arith  a 128-bit integer, as SKIPS.spirv.
int128/mul  a 128-bit integer, as SKIPS.spirv.
int128/convert_int128  a 128-bit integer, as SKIPS.spirv.
int128/cmp_int128  a 128-bit integer, as SKIPS.spirv.
int128/call_int128  a 128-bit integer, as SKIPS.spirv.
int128/divrem  a 128-bit integer, as SKIPS.spirv.
int128/shift  a 128-bit integer, as SKIPS.spirv.
int128/call_vector  a 128-bit integer, as SKIPS.spirv.
int128/vector_reinterpret  a 128-bit integer, as SKIPS.spirv.
mem/global_data  a plain module-scope variable, as SKIPS.spirv.
mem/escaping_element  pointer arithmetic across whole objects, as SKIPS.spirv.
mem/global_zero  a plain module-scope variable, as SKIPS.spirv.
mem/agg_overlap  pointer arithmetic across whole objects, as SKIPS.spirv.
mem/ptr_arith  pointer arithmetic across whole objects, as SKIPS.spirv.
vec/load_literal  pointer arithmetic across whole objects, as SKIPS.spirv.
vec/range  pointer arithmetic across whole objects, as SKIPS.spirv.
vec/split  pointer arithmetic across whole objects, as SKIPS.spirv.
vec/wide_rows  pointer arithmetic across whole objects, as SKIPS.spirv.
vec/global_loop  pointer arithmetic across whole objects, as SKIPS.spirv.
mem/uni_layout  a raw union parameter, as SKIPS.spirv.

# ---- MACH DEFECT ----
